Title: Scottish Open: Rory McIlroy happy & ready for Portrush despite near miss
Date: 2025-07-13
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': '"No frustration; it\'s been a great week," he said of four rounds that concluded with him 13-under par after 19 birdies across the week.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 119}}, {'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': '"I\'m really happy with where my game is; the way I played over the weekend; the shots that I hit, how I controlled my ball flight. Missing the trophy, that\'s about it."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 144}}, {'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': '"It was pretty windy and was hard to get the ball super close, but I gave myself plenty of chances coming down the stretch," the Northern Irishman said.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 9, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 126}}, {'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': '"I feel like the greens got a little bumpy. I had some good putts that just didn\'t go in, whether they were mis-reads or poor speed.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 10, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 119}}, {'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': '"But I feel like I\'ve gotten out of this week what I wanted. I\'m looking forward to getting to Portrush tonight and getting out on to the golf course early tomorrow."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 11, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 152}}], 'Description': [], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'Rory McIlroy'}]}
